From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: set the macroblock rate control and the GOP
 length separately

configureDevice() sets V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_MB_RC_ENABLE and a GOP length
of 0 in one VIDIOC_S_EXT_CTRLS call and ignores the result. The call
applies all of its controls or none, so on a device without
MB_RC_ENABLE, such as Qualcomm iris, the GOP length stays at the
driver's default, 30 on iris gen1. The firmware then adds an intra
frame every 30 frames between the key frames the component requests at
the configured interval. A screen recording at 120 fps with a 2 s
interval got non-IDR I-frames at frames 30, 60, ..., 210 between the
IDRs at 0 and 240, and they took about a sixth of the bytes.

Set the two controls in separate calls. For the GOP length, query the
control's range first: the control framework clamps an integer to the
range instead of rejecting it, so a device whose minimum is 1 would
silently get a GOP length of 1, a key frame on every frame. Such a
device, or one that rejects 0, gets the longest GOP length it supports;
a device without the control is left alone. A negative key frame
interval gives a key frame period of 0, which the counter divided by
and initialize() asserted against; treat it as "the first frame and
requested key frames only".

On iris gen1 this also needs the driver to honour a GOP length of 0
("media: iris: gen1: honour a GOP size of 0"). Without that fix the
driver accepts the control, drops it when streaming starts, and the
firmware codes every frame as an intra frame.

Checked on SC8280XP (Huawei MateBook E Go) with that kernel fix:
300-frame HEVC and H.264 encodes at 30 fps with a 5 s key frame interval
have key frames at frames 0 and 150 only, and with a negative interval
at frame 0 only; before, both had a key frame every 30 frames.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 v4l2/V4L2Encoder.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v4l2/V4L2Encoder.cpp b/v4l2/V4L2Encoder.cpp
index 172c9ba..d5adf3b 100644
--- a/v4l2/V4L2Encoder.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2Encoder.cpp
@@ -215,7 +215,6 @@ bool V4L2Encoder::initialize(C2Config::profile_t outputProfile, std::optional<ui
                              std::optional<uint32_t> peakBitrate) {
     ALOGV("%s()", __func__);
     ALOG_ASSERT(mTaskRunner->RunsTasksInCurrentSequence());
-    ALOG_ASSERT(keyFramePeriod > 0);
 
     mVisibleSize = visibleSize;
     mKeyFramePeriod = keyFramePeriod;
@@ -323,7 +322,9 @@ void V4L2Encoder::handleEncodeRequest() {
             return;
         }
     }
-    mKeyFrameCounter = (mKeyFrameCounter + 1) % mKeyFramePeriod;
+    // A period of 0 (negative key frame interval) asks for no periodic key frames: only the first
+    // frame and the frames requested through requestKeyframe() are key frames.
+    mKeyFrameCounter = mKeyFramePeriod > 0 ? (mKeyFrameCounter + 1) % mKeyFramePeriod : 1;
 
     // Enqueue the input frame in the V4L2 device.
     uint64_t index = encodeRequest.video_frame->index();
@@ -612,11 +613,30 @@ bool V4L2Encoder::configureDevice(C2Config::profile_t outputProfile,
         // assume the operation was successful for now.
     }
 
-    // Additional optional controls:
+    // Additional optional controls, each set on its own: VIDIOC_S_EXT_CTRLS applies all controls of
+    // a call or none, so a control the device lacks would take the others with it.
     // - Enable macroblock-level bitrate control.
-    // - Set GOP length to 0 to disable periodic key frames.
-    mDevice->setExtCtrls(V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_MPEG, {V4L2ExtCtrl(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_MB_RC_ENABLE, 1),
-                                                V4L2ExtCtrl(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_GOP_SIZE, 0)});
+    if (!mDevice->setExtCtrls(V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_MPEG,
+                              {V4L2ExtCtrl(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_MB_RC_ENABLE, 1)})) {
+        ALOGV("Device doesn't support macroblock-level bitrate control");
+    }
+    // - Disable periodic key frames: we request key frames ourselves. The control framework clamps
+    //   an integer to the control's range instead of rejecting it, so check the range first: a
+    //   device whose GOP length starts at 1 would otherwise code every frame as a key frame. Such a
+    //   device, or one that rejects 0, gets the longest GOP length it supports.
+    struct v4l2_query_ext_ctrl gopCtrl;
+    memset(&gopCtrl, 0, sizeof(gopCtrl));
+    gopCtrl.id = V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_GOP_SIZE;
+    if (mDevice->ioctl(VIDIOC_QUERY_EXT_CTRL, &gopCtrl) != 0) {
+        ALOGV("Device doesn't support setting the GOP length");
+    } else if ((gopCtrl.minimum > 0 ||
+                !mDevice->setExtCtrls(V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_MPEG,
+                                      {V4L2ExtCtrl(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_GOP_SIZE, 0)})) &&
+               !mDevice->setExtCtrls(V4L2_CTRL_CLASS_MPEG,
+                                     {V4L2ExtCtrl(V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_GOP_SIZE,
+                                                  static_cast<int32_t>(gopCtrl.maximum))})) {
+        ALOGW("Failed to disable periodic key frames on the device");
+    }
 
     // All controls below are codec-specific.
     if (outputProfile >= C2Config::PROFILE_AVC_BASELINE &&
